    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12574v2</id>
    <title>L(3,2,1)-labelings of three classes of 4-valent circulants</title>
    <updated>2026-05-12T16:38:31Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.12574v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2601.12574v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>An $L(3,2,1)$-labeling of a graph $G$ is an assignment $f$ of nonnegative integers to vertices such that $\vert f(x)-f(y)\vert &gt; 3-\mbox{dist}_G(x,y)$ for every pair $x,y$ of vertices of $G$, where $\mbox{dist}_G(x,y)$ denotes the distance between $x$ and $y$ in $G$. The minimum span (i.e., the difference between the largest and the smallest value) among all $L(3,2,1)$-labelings of $G$ is denoted by $λ_{(3,2,1)}(G)$. In this paper, we study $L(3,2,1)$-labelings of three classes of circulant graphs. Namely, we investigate $λ_{(3,2,1)}$ of circulant graphs $C_n(1,t)$, where $t\in\{3,4,5\}$ and $n$ is the order of the graph. This paper is a continuation of a recent publications of V. Bianco and T. Calamoneri who studied the square of cycles, i.e., circulant graphs $C_n(1,2)$.</summary>
